event: text
data: {"node":"look","run":"f91ea4dc2dfe7820cd3523642391e2ce","text":"The page that answers this directly, `cold-chain-r6` (Cold-chain excursion response, revision 6), is **superseded** — do not answer from it. Its replacement is `cold-chain-r7` (Cold-chain excursion response, revision 7), current, which states what changed: re-ice at the nearest hub first and do not wait for the consignee to answer, because the telemetry reading is the evidence and it is kept for us; the notification window is **ninety minutes**, not four hours; form CX-11 is retired — raise an Excursion ticket in Dockside instead and attach the reading to that (`cold-chain-r7`).\n\nTwo hours above the set band qualifies as an excursion under `reefer-telemetry` (current): a reading outside the set band for more than twenty consecutive minutes is logged as an excursion, with the first and last minute of it; a container that stops reporting is not an excursion and is handled as a telemetry fault (`reefer-telemetry`).\n\nSo: the superseded page's four-hour window and CX-11 form no longer apply; the current response is re-ice at the nearest hub immediately (no waiting on the consignee), raise an Excursion ticket in Dockside with the reading attached, and notify the consignee within ninety minutes of the excursion being logged (`cold-chain-r7`), the excursion being established per `reefer-telemetry`."}

